# DS41RT example: 1 RTX + 3 Spark, official native checkpoint, TP3 x EP1.
#
# ============================================================================
# V10 CANDIDATE PROFILE - NOT RELEASE-QUALIFIED. This opt-in overlay is
# launcher support for the explicit `TP3xEP1` geometry: three Spark ranks form
# ONE unreplicated group (EP1 means a single group, no duplication). The
# daemon, transport, N-plane reduction and the SM121 `spark_tp3` expert role
# already exist and ship in the universal release pair, but nothing here
# establishes quality, memory, performance or readiness for this three-rank
# layout; the earlier TP3xEP2 experiments recorded a strict quality FAIL.
# This file targets the v10 release pair and is not selected automatically.
# ============================================================================
#
#   ./run.sh --config examples/configs/tp3ep1-native.config --dry-run
#
# group = rank / 3, tp_rank = rank % 3, so every rank is in group 0:
#   ostrich,dodo,emu -> group 0, tp_rank 0,1,2

MODEL_ID=deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
MODEL_VARIANT=flash
MODEL_REVISION=dba1be0a40aa45a94ad051997016db3960a90277
EXPERT_FORMAT=native
SPARKINFER_EXL3=disable
EXL3_PAIRED_TP4=off

RTX_GPUS=1
# All 40 routed layers stay remote: `0` is pinned deliberately so this
# candidate has one unambiguous all-remote shape. A single RTX `auto` launch
# has no local boundary to publish and keeps the no-handoff launch; explicit
# local counts 1..39 are supported through the coordinator-published placement
# plan on an explicit topology.
RTX_EXPERT_LAYERS=0

# Explicit keys are mandatory for a native three-rank launch: count 3 without
# them is the compact EXL3 TP3 profile, never this one.
SPARK_COUNT=3
SPARK_TP=3
SPARK_EP=1

SPARK_0_HOST=ostrich
SPARK_1_HOST=dodo
SPARK_2_HOST=emu
SPARK_0_LANE_A=10.55.0.1
SPARK_1_LANE_A=10.55.0.2
SPARK_2_LANE_A=10.55.0.3

# v10 target images. The universal role set advertises tp2;tp3;tp6, and
# `run.sh` selects the `tp3` expert role this topology needs; the published
# v9 pair already carries it, so point both names at the v10 pair on release.
COORDINATOR_DOCKER_INFERENCE=ghcr.io/tpurtell/ds41rt-coordinator:v10
SPARK_EXPERT_DOCKER_INFERENCE=ghcr.io/tpurtell/ds41rt-spark-expert:v10

# Budget: TP3 per-rank layer bytes are the exact 2304/3 = 768-column shard,
# 40 * 2,406,481,920 = 96,259,276,800 B for all layers. This is the live
# three-host floor: min(MemTotal) over ostrich/dodo/emu (127,533,356 kB,
# read 2026-09-21) * 1024 - 20 GiB = 109,119,320,064 B, identical to the
# six-host tested floor because dodo is the minimum. Weight-only admission is
# not a launch-feasibility claim: workspace, load staging and runtime headroom
# are only known when the expert service reports them.
SPARK_DEVICE_BUDGET_BYTES=109119320064
